    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d792">

                <pb facs="1552" n="1512" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884A.86/4–1254: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 792<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Department
                        of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d792-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-04-12T10:00:00+01:00">April 12, 1954—10
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4489. I mentioned to Eden last evening Churchill’s message to Sharett (Deptel
                    5344 to London)<anchor n="2" xml:id="d792-f2"/> and discussed possibility of my
                    sending similar message. Eden unaware UK Embassy instructed to tell us about
                    Churchill’s message. He said that since Churchill considered pro-Zionist a
                    message from him had seemed desirable but doubted desirability of supporting
                    message from US.</p>
                <p>In view of above and fact that further message from me might be construed as
                    resulting from my visit London rather than from our own initiative do not
                    believe we should send any message at this time.</p>
                <closer><signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
